This package contains original, machine-assisted reformulations of methodologies and decision
frameworks derived from the Russian edition of “Fundamentals of Software Architecture” by Mark
Richards and Neal Ford, ISBN 978-601-12-6107-4. The original English edition is published by
O'Reilly Media and is copyright © 2020 Mark Richards and Neal Ford. All rights in the source book,
its translation, figures, examples, trademarks, and trade dress remain with their respective owners.

The owner recorded the public-distribution decision at CP5 in `sources.json`. The source PDF and
extracted corpus are not included. This package SHIPS a mechanical word-shingling gate
(`scripts/shingling-check.mjs`) that compares a public artifact with a source corpus and rejects
uncited verbatim runs of eight or more words. HONEST CORRECTION, replacing an earlier claim in this
file that the gate runs before release: no run of that gate against THIS pack is recorded anywhere —
not in `sources.json`, not in `CP4-PACK-REPORT.md`, not in `test/pack.test.mjs` — and the gate is not
invoked by `prepublishOnly`. The corpus it would need is owner-local and is not distributed, so the
run cannot be reproduced from this package either. The paraphrase discipline behind these
reformulations is therefore authorial and reviewed, not mechanically attested for this pack; the
sibling pack `@dzhechkov/skills-book-ai-apps` carries dated runs of the same gate and its LICENSE
states them. Treat this paragraph as a description of what exists, not as a licence or legal opinion.

You may install and use this package, including commercially, and quote short attributed passages
